{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/notes/cic_roundchain.tex","new_string":"\\section{The $3$-smooth cascade and the $2$-adic logarithm calculus}\n\nThe Mersenne theorem extends to the full $3$-smooth neighborhoods\n$x=2^g3^a\\mp1$ --- and the cascade goes \\emph{deeper} than one round.\nAll statements below are machine-verified\n(\\texttt{search/smooth\\_cascade.py}; grids $g<42$, $a<26$, and the\none-parameter family to $n\\le3000$).\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Minus family]\\label{thm:minus}\nFor $x=2^g3^a-1$ ($g\\ge2$) the entire round chain depends on $(g,a)$\nonly through $n=g+a-1$ (the chain sees $m,\\ell$ only through\n$3^\\ell m=3^n$). The first reading is $v=\\vt(3^n-1)$, given by LTE:\n$v=1$ for $n$ odd, $v=2+\\vt(n)$ for $n$ even; survival iff $\\vt(n)$\nis even $\\ge2$, of density $\\tfrac16$ over $n$ --- the family is\nghost-aligned and dies at $2\\times$ the Haar rate in round one. The\nround-$2$ reading is the $4$-term $S$-unit valuation\n\\[\nv'=\\vt\\bigl(3^{\\,n+r+\\ell'}-3^{\\,r+\\ell'}+2^{v}3^{\\ell'}-2^{\\,v+\\ell'}\\bigr)\n-v-\\ell' .\n\\]\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Plus family]\\label{thm:plus}\nFor $x=2^g3^a+1$ ($g\\ge3$) the $+1$ clock rides\n$\\lfloor(g-1)/2\\rfloor$ blocks ending $3$-smooth, with\n$a'=a+\\lfloor(g-1)/2\\rfloor$:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[(i)] $g$ even: terminal $4\\cdot3^{a'}+1$, death letter\n$b=2+\\vt(3^{a'+1}+1)\\in\\{3,4\\}$ by LTE --- closed-form CIC death.\n\\item[(ii)] $g$ odd: lands at $2\\cdot3^{a'}+1$, next depth $g'=2$\n($a'$ even) or $3$ ($a'$ odd). If $a'$ is even the round-$2$ reading\nis $v'=\\vt(3^{a'+1}+1)-1=1$: closed-form death. If $a'$ is odd,\n\\[\nv'=\\vt\\bigl(3^{a'+2}+5\\bigr)-2\n=\\vt\\bigl(a'+2-\\mathrm{Log}_3(-5)\\bigr):\n\\]\n\\emph{the survival reading is the $2$-adic alignment of the exponent\nto the $2$-adic logarithm of the ghost $-5$}, where\n$N_0=\\mathrm{Log}_3(-5)=2556611305511861515 \\bmod 2^{64}$ and\n$\\vt(3^N+5)=2+\\vt(N-N_0)$ for $N\\equiv N_0\\bmod2$.\n\\end{itemize}\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{proposition}[The $S$-unit horizon]\\label{prop:horizon}\nAlong any $3$-smooth-seeded chain, the round-$j$ reading is the\n$2$-adic valuation of a $2$--$3$ $S$-unit form whose term count grows\nwith $j$; two-term forms are LTE (closed), and the collapsed cases\nreduce to alignments of integer exponents to $2$-adic logarithms of\nghosts. The deterministic horizon of the cascade is exactly the\n$S$-unit term count the machinery can close --- the CIC on these\nfamilies meets the banded $S$-unit frontier (Target 1) at the level of\n\\emph{exponents}, where effective $p$-adic Baker theory (Yu) bounds\nevery reading by $O(\\log)$ of the exponent height.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\noindent\\emph{Cascade statistics} (one-parameter family, $n\\le3000$):\nsurvival $0.16633$ after round $1$ (LTE prediction $\\tfrac16$), then\nconditional survivals $0.34,\\ 0.31,\\ 0.40,\\ 0.19,\\ 0.25$ --- the\nre-randomized fair-thirds coin of \\cref{thm:iid}. The champion is\n$n=704$, surviving $6$ rounds with readings $[8,2,2,2,2,2,3]$;\n\\emph{every} $n\\le3000$ dies by round $7$: the CIC holds, with\nexplicit finite certificates, for the entire $3$-smooth slice tested.\nThe ghost hierarchy thus lifts one level: at the base, integers align\nto ghosts ($-1$, $+1$, $-5$, \\dots); at the exponent level, exponents\nalign to $2$-adic logarithms of ghosts; survival is a parity reading\nat each level, deterministic exactly where freshness fails.\n\n\\section{Where the wall now stands}","old_string":"\\section{Where the wall now stands}","replace_all":false}